<office:text>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://example.com" office:name="">
<text:span text:style-name="Definition"> linked body </text:span>
</text:a> keeps the padding of its content.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A box holds its own spacing within the line.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">An underlined <text:span text:style-name="T1"> padded body </text:span> sits beside plain words.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Quotations">A spaced quotation.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Quotations">—  A. Author </text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="First_20_paragraph">A footnote body is trimmed <text:note text:id="ftn0" text:note-class="footnote">
<text:note-citation>1</text:note-citation>
<text:note-body>
<text:p text:style-name="Footnote">Trimmed on both ends.</text:p>
</text:note-body>
</text:note> here.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="FigureWithCaption">
</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="FigureCaption">Figure caption.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Loop rounds join with their padding: 1 2 3 .</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A measurement of 6.0em, a ratio of 50%, and 1.5e-2 exact.</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">
</text:p>
<text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The binding kept survives its statement.</text:p>
</office:text>
